ol": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_malformed"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 377331, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KvKnvyyoCmUo9NFxNScySq", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380910, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened a pull request against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` says in its comment that it uses banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why the test expecting `2.665` to round to `2.66` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed one line so it uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018VPzhgVPtCPvbptwVZ3bQC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019Go1KJnMauJ5m3WwTP2yEQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CrYtzxKexaTJDcLpkDfmSq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QuqicDsKbVoznzfp33DNzy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017PheEifnuY5KpDd